<!-- SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Johannes Meyer zum Alten Borgloh
     SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

     The Sailfish OS side of the pdx246 port: the adaptation repos at the paths the HADK
     scripts expect, the middleware with this port's fixes, and the default middleware pinned
     to the commits the port is built and tested with. build_packages.sh -o builds what is
     checked out here and only clones what is missing.
     libhybris' submodule (the source) comes from github.com/sailfishos-sony-pdx246/libhybris-source;
     droid-bthelper needs its tag 0.3.0 (build_packages.sh -o derives the version from it).
     waydroid is sailfishos-open's packaging: upstream 1.6.3 as submodule (waydroid/waydroid at
     the tag), the port's patches in rpm/ (build-packages-sdk.sh step waydroid applies them).
     waydroid-runner is sailfishos-open's runner with the port's background mode (Android keeps
     running when its window is closed, a setting can make closing stop it), Android apps'
     launchers and Android's setup at the first start. Both are in the image, with Waydroid's
     dependencies that Jolla's repositories do not have: gbinder-python (sailfishos-chum's
     packaging with the port's spec fix), dnsmasq-pdx246 (the port's packaging of dnsmasq; not
     hybris/mw/dnsmasq, which build_packages.sh would take for AOSP's external/dnsmasq) and
     waydroid-sensors (sailfishos-open's packaging, unchanged). -->
